  "Partitions": {
    "not/1": "Exactly true/false atoms are accepted and negated; every other term raises badarg. Canonical Boolean atoms are returned with no input mutation.",
    "and/2": "Both arguments must be true/false atoms. The exhaustive four-case truth table matches OTP; either invalid argument raises badarg, including false in first position. Eager native BIF semantics, not short-circuit source syntax.",
    "or/2": "Both arguments must be true/false atoms. The exhaustive four-case truth table matches OTP; either invalid argument raises badarg, including true in first position. Eager native BIF semantics.",
    "xor/2": "Both arguments must be true/false atoms. Return true iff they differ; either invalid argument raises badarg. Canonical atom result.",
    "+/1": "Integer or finite FloatTerm returns the exact supplied term without allocation or conversion. Every other term raises badarith.",
    "-/1": "Integer negation is exact arbitrary-precision subtraction from zero, including small/big boundaries; finite float negation flips its sign including both zeros and subnormals, creating a fresh float. All other terms raise badarith.",
    "bnot/1": "Integer-only infinite signed two-complement complement equals -x-1 for all integer magnitudes/signs. Small/big representations preserve the value and fresh boxed-result semantics. Noninteger terms raise badarith. No claim of identical VM physical allocation limits."
  },
